#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:4
msgid "CMakeConfigDeps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../common/experimental_warning.inc:3
msgid ""
"This feature is experimental and subject to breaking changes. See :ref:`the "
"Conan stability<stability>` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:9
msgid ""
"This generator (available as experimental from Conan 2.25) is designed as a "
"replacement of the current ``CMakeDeps`` generator, with multiple pending "
"fixes and improvements that couldn't easily be done in the current one "
"without breaking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:13
msgid ""
"To simplify the testing and validation of the ``CMakeDeps`` -> "
"``CMakeConfigDeps`` migration, the ``-c "
"tools.cmake.cmakedeps:new=will_break_next`` configuration can be used. It "
"performs a hot replacement of every ``CMakeDeps`` in recipes by "
"``CMakeConfigDeps``, without needing to edit the recipes at all. Note that "
"this configuration is not necessary if the recipe explicitly uses "
"``CMakeConfigDeps``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:17
msgid ""
"That means that it can be used as any other generator in conanfiles, and in "
"command line ``-g CMakeConfigDeps``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:19
msgid "conanfile.txt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:19
msgid ""
"[requires]\n"
"hello/0.1\n"
"\n"
"[generators]\n"
"CMakeConfigDeps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:29
#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:39
#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:324
#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:369
#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:425
msgid "conanfile.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:29
msgid ""
"class Pkg(ConanFile):\n"
"   ...\n"
"   requires = \"hello/0.1\"\n"
"   generators = \"CMakeConfigDeps\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:37
msgid "Or:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:39
msgid ""
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"from conan.tools.cmake import CMakeConfigDeps\n"
"\n"
"class TestConan(ConanFile):\n"
"   ...\n"
"   requires = \"hello/0.1\"\n"
"\n"
"   def generate(self):\n"
"      deps = CMakeConfigDeps(self)\n"
"      deps.generate()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:54
msgid ""
"The ``CMakeConfigDeps`` generator produces the necessary files for each "
"dependency to be able to use the cmake ``find_package()`` function to locate "
"the dependencies. It can be used like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:57
msgid "**CMakeLists.txt**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:57
msgid ""
"cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.15)\n"
"project(compressor C)\n"
"\n"
"find_package(hello CONFIG REQUIRED)\n"
"\n"
"add_executable(${PROJECT_NAME} src/main.c)\n"
"target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME} hello::hello)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:70
msgid ""
"By default, for a ``hello`` requires, you need to use "
"``find_package(hello)`` and link with the target ``hello::hello``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:74
msgid "Generated files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:76
msgid ""
"**xxx-config.cmake**: By default, the ``CMakeConfigDeps`` generator will "
"create config files declaring the targets for the dependencies and their "
"components (if declared)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:79
msgid ""
"This generator is only intended to generate ``xxx-config.cmake`` config "
"files, it will not generate ``Find*.cmake`` find modules, and support for it "
"is not planned. Use the ``CMakeDeps`` generator for that, or patch the "
"consumers to use CMake config files instead of modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:81
msgid ""
"**Other necessary *.cmake**:  files like version, flags and directory data "
"or configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:83
msgid ""
"**conan_cmakedeps_paths.cmake**: file containing the definition of "
"``xxx_DIR`` variables that point to the folder containing the ``xxx-"
"config.cmake`` files to be located when doing the ``find_package()``. This "
"file will be included by default by the ``conan_toolchain.cmake``, but it "
"might also be useful in other tools like ``cmake-conan`` integration. This "
"file will also contain other path variables such as "
"``CMAKE_VS_DEBUGGER_ENVIRONMENT``, ``CMAKE_PROGRAM_PATH``, "
"``CMAKE_LIBRARY_PATH``, etc., that help consumers to locate dependencies for "
"different scenarios like runtime or with other CMake ``find_program()`` "
"utilities. It also prepends the package folders of the dependencies to "
"``CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH``, as a fallback for the cases not covered by the "
"``<pkg>_DIR`` variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:93
msgid "Improvements over ``CMakeDeps``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:95
msgid ""
"This is a brief summary of the improvements and fixes of ``CMakeConfigDeps`` "
"over ``CMakeDeps``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:97
msgid ""
"Creates real ``SHARED/STATIC/INTERFACE IMPORTED`` targets, no more "
"artificial interface targets. The ``CONAN_LIB::`` and other similar targets "
"do not exist anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:98
msgid "Defines ``IMPORTED_CONFIGURATIONS`` for targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:99
msgid ""
"``CONFIG`` definition of dependencies matching the dependency ``Release/"
"Debug/etc`` ``build_type``, no longer using the consumer one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:100
msgid ""
"Definition of ``IMPORTED_LOCATION`` and ``IMPORTED_IMPLIB`` for library "
"targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:101
msgid ""
"Definition of ``LINK_LANGUAGES`` based on the recipe ``languages`` and "
"``cpp_info/component`` ``languages`` properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:102
msgid ""
"All these allows better propagation of linkage requirement and visibility, "
"avoiding some linkage error of transitive shared libraries in Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:103
msgid ""
"Better definition of ``requires`` relationships across components inside the "
"same package and with respect to other packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:104
msgid ""
"It doesn't need any ``build_context_activated`` or ``build_context_suffix`` "
"to use ``tool_requires`` dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:105
msgid "Checking CMake ``COMPONENTS`` definition by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:106
msgid ""
"Definition of ``cpp_info/components`` ``.exe`` information (should include "
"the ``.location`` definition too), to define ``EXECUTABLE`` targets that can "
"be run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:107
msgid ""
"Executables from ``requires`` can also be used in non cross-build scenarios. "
"When a ``tool_requires`` to the same dependency exists, then those "
"executables will have priority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:108
msgid ""
"Creation of a new ``conan_cmakedeps_paths.cmake`` that contains definitions "
"of ``<pkg>_DIR`` paths for direct finding of the dependencies. This file is "
"also planned to be used in ``cmake-conan`` to extend its usage and avoid "
"some current limitations due to the fact that a CMake driven installation "
"cannot inject a toolchain later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:109
msgid ""
"Better management of the system OSX Frameworks through "
"``cpp_info.frameworks``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:110
msgid ""
"Definition of ``cpp_info/component.package_framework`` information (should "
"include the ``.location`` definition too, e.g., "
"``os.path.join(self.package_folder, \"MyFramework.framework\", "
"\"MyFramework\")``) to define the custom OSX Framework library to be linked "
"against."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:112
msgid ""
"Definition of ``self.cpp_info.sources = [\"src/mylib.cpp\", \"src/"
"other.cpp\"]`` that will add ``INTERFACE_SOURCES`` to the CMake target to be "
"consumed downstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:117
msgid "Targets generation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:119
msgid ""
"``CMakeConfigDeps`` can both generate CMake files from the dependencies "
"``package_info()`` information or use the in-package ``xxx-config.cmake`` "
"files (when ``self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_find_mode\", \"none\")`` is "
"defined, that indicates that the generator will not create any files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:122
msgid ""
"This section explains how ``CMakeConfigDeps`` generates CMake targets from "
"the information of the ``package_info()`` dependencies method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:125
msgid "cpp_info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:127
msgid ""
"``CMakeConfigDeps`` will use the "
"common :ref:`self.cpp_info<conan_conanfile_model_cppinfo>` fields, like "
"``includedirs``, ``libs``, etc. to create and populate the targets the "
"consumers will use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:130
msgid ""
"But besides these common fields, there are a few new fields, exclusively "
"used at the moment by ``CMakeConfigDeps``, that implement some of the new "
"capabilities of this generator that can be defined in the ``cpp_info`` or "
"``cpp_info.components``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:132
msgid ""
"# EXPERIMENTAL FIELDS, used exclusively by new CMakeConfigDeps\n"
"self.cpp_info.type  # The type of this artifact \"shared-library\", \"static-"
"library\", etc (same as package_type)\n"
"self.cpp_info.location # full location (path and filename with extension) of "
"the artifact or the Apple Framework library one\n"
"self.cpp_info.link_location  # Location of the import library for "
"Windows .lib associated to a dll\n"
"self.cpp_info.languages # same as \"languages\" attribute, it can be \"C\", "
"\"C++\"\n"
"self.cpp_info.exe  # Definition of an executable artifact\n"
"self.cpp_info.package_framework  # Definition of an Apple Framework (new "
"since Conan 2.14)\n"
"self.cpp_info.sources  # List of paths to source files in the package (for "
"packages that provide source code to consumers)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:144
msgid ""
"These fields will be auto-deduced from the other ``cpp_info`` and "
"``components`` definitions, like the ``libs`` or ``libdirs`` fields, but the "
"automatic deduction might have limitations. Defining them explicitly will "
"inhibit the auto deduction and use the value as provided by the recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:146
msgid "Declare sources for targets with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:148
msgid "self.cpp_info.sources = [\"src/mylib.cpp\", \"src/other.cpp\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:152
msgid ""
"This allows packages to provide source code as a dependency to consumers. "
"The paths should be relative to the package folder. The source files will be "
"added as `INTERFACE_SOURCES` property to the CMake library (or component) "
"target and consumers that link with this target will compile the sources "
"when building their own targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:158
msgid ""
"A package (or component) that only declares ``cpp_info.sources``, without "
"any other field like ``includedirs`` or ``libs``, will still get an "
"``INTERFACE`` CMake target created for it (since Conan 2.33). Previously, "
"packages that exclusively provided sources and nothing else were skipped, "
"and no target was generated for them at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:162
msgid ""
"``INTERFACE_SOURCES`` are only set on the target when the package declaring "
"them is a **direct** dependency of the consumer for which the files are "
"being generated (since Conan 2.33). If the package is only reachable "
"transitively (for example, through another dependency using "
"``transitive_headers``/``transitive_libs``), its target can still be "
"generated, but without the ``INTERFACE_SOURCES`` property, to avoid the same "
"sources being unexpectedly compiled more than once through different paths "
"of the dependency graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:170
msgid "Filtering of the target information based on requires traits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:172
msgid ""
"Since Conan 2.34, ``CMakeConfigDeps`` filters the information injected in "
"the generated targets according to "
"the :ref:`traits<reference_conanfile_methods_requirements>` (``headers``, "
"``libs``, ``run``...) of the requirement as seen from the consumer, so that "
"consumers do not get compile and link information from dependencies that "
"they do not really need to compile or link against. This is the same kind of "
"filtering that ``CMakeDeps`` does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:177
msgid ""
"If ``headers=False``, the header-related information is not injected: "
"``includedirs`` and ``defines``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:178
msgid ""
"If ``headers=False`` and ``libs=False``, the remaining compile and link "
"information is not injected either: ``cxxflags``, ``cflags``, "
"``sharedlinkflags``, ``exelinkflags`` and ``system_libs``. This is typically "
"the case of a requirement that is only needed at runtime, like ``run=True``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:181
msgid ""
"If ``libs=False``, but ``headers=True``, the ``system_libs`` and the link "
"flags of the dependency are still injected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:183
msgid ""
"For Apple ``package_framework``, the framework information is only injected "
"if ``headers=True`` or ``libs=True``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:185
msgid "Some information is **not** filtered by the traits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:187
msgid ""
"The target is always declared, even if it ends up with no compile or link "
"information, so that it can still be depended upon by other targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:189
msgid ""
"The ``IMPORTED_LOCATION`` (and ``IMPORTED_IMPLIB``) and the type of the "
"library targets are always defined, even for ``libs=False``. For example, if "
"``engine`` is a shared library that privately links ``matrix`` "
"(``transitive_libs=False``), an application requiring ``engine`` doesn't "
"link ``matrix`` directly, but the Linux linker still needs to locate "
"``libmatrix.so`` when linking against ``libengine.so``, so the location of "
"``matrix`` is necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:194
msgid ""
"The ``cpp_info.sources`` are not filtered by ``headers`` or ``libs``; they "
"follow the direct dependency rule explained above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:201
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:203
msgid "The following properties affect the ``CMakeConfigDeps`` generator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:205
msgid ""
"**cmake_file_name**: The config file generated for the current package will "
"follow the ``<VALUE>-config.cmake`` pattern, so to find the package you "
"write ``find_package(<VALUE>)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:207
msgid ""
"**cmake_file_names**: Dictionary to split a package into **several** CMake "
"config files, each one containing a subset of the package components. The "
"keys are the names of the CMake packages (the ``<KEY>-config.cmake`` files, "
"found with ``find_package(<KEY>)``) and the values are dictionaries with the "
"following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:211
msgid ""
"``components``: list of the package component names that belong to that "
"config file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:212
msgid ""
"``properties`` (optional): dictionary of properties that apply only to that "
"config file, overriding the package-level ones. For example "
"``system_package_version``, ``cmake_config_version_compat``, "
"``cmake_build_modules``, ``cmake_extra_variables``, "
"``cmake_additional_variables_prefixes``, ``cmake_extra_dependencies`` or "
"``cmake_file_name_variants``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:217
msgid ""
"See :ref:`CMakeConfigDeps multiple config "
"files<cmakeconfigdeps_multiple_config_files>` for the details and "
"limitations. This property is only available since Conan 2.34, it takes "
"precedence over **cmake_file_name** (which is ignored if both are defined), "
"and it cannot be set from the consumer for ``build_context=True`` "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:220
msgid ""
"**cmake_file_name_variants**: List of upper/lower case variants of the cmake "
"file name that consumers can use to find the package. This is useful to "
"increase the compatibility with different CMake ``find_package()`` calls "
"that might be used in the consumers. An error will be raised if the list "
"contains words that are not variants of the ``cmake_file_name`` value unless "
"the consumer explicitly sets a custom ``cmake_file_name``, in which case the "
"variants will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:224
msgid "**cmake_target_name**: Name of the target to be consumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:225
msgid ""
"**cmake_target_aliases**: List of aliases that Conan will create for an "
"already existing target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:226
msgid "**cmake_find_mode**: Defaulted to ``config``. Possible values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:228
msgid ""
"``config``: The ``CMakeConfigDeps`` generator will create config scripts for "
"the dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:229
msgid ""
"``module``: Not supported, will be ignored and generate only ``xxx-"
"config.cmake`` files (with a warning)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:230
msgid ""
"``both``: Not supported, will be ignored and generate only ``xxx-"
"config.cmake`` files (with a warning)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:231
msgid ""
"``none``: Won't generate any file. It can be used, for instance, to create a "
"system wrapper package so the consumers find the config files in the CMake "
"installation config path and not in the generated by Conan (because it has "
"been skipped)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:232
msgid ""
"**cmake_build_modules**: List of ``.cmake`` files (path relative to root "
"package folder) that are automatically included when the consumer run the "
"``find_package()``. This property cannot be set in the components, only in "
"the root ``self.cpp_info``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:234
msgid ""
"**cmake_config_version_compat**: By default ``SameMajorVersion``, it can "
"take the values ``\"AnyNewerVersion\", \"SameMajorVersion\", "
"\"SameMinorVersion\", \"ExactVersion\"``. It will use that policy in the "
"generated ``<PackageName>ConfigVersion.cmake`` file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:235
msgid ""
"**system_package_version**: version of the package used to generate the "
"``<PackageName>ConfigVersion.cmake`` file. Can be useful when creating "
"system packages or other wrapper packages, where the conan package version "
"is different to the eventually referenced package version to keep "
"compatibility to ``find_package(<PackageName> <Version>)`` calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:236
msgid ""
"**cmake_additional_variables_prefixes**: List of prefixes to be used when "
"creating CMake variables in the config files. These variables are created "
"with ``file_name`` as prefix by default, but setting this property will "
"create additional variables with the specified prefixes alongside the "
"default ``file_name`` one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:239
msgid ""
"**cmake_extra_variables**: Dictionary of extra variables to be added to the "
"generated config file. The keys of the dictionary are the variable names and "
"the values are the variable values, which can be a plain string, a number or "
"a dict-like python object which must specify the ``value`` (string/number) , "
"``cache`` (boolean), ``type`` (CMake cache type) and optionally, "
"``docstring`` (string: defaulted to variable name) and ``force`` (boolean) "
"keys. Note that this has less preference over those values defined in the "
"``tools.cmake.cmaketoolchain:extra_variables`` conf."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:245
msgid ""
"**cmake_extra_dependencies**: List of extra package names for which a "
"``find_dependency()`` call will be added to the generated ``<pkg>-"
"config.cmake`` file. Useful when the package depends on libraries located "
"via CMake's ``find_package()`` but not declared as Conan ``requires`` (for "
"example, system-provided dependencies like ``OpenMPI``). This property is "
"only honored at the package level (setting it on a component has no effect)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:250
msgid ""
"**cmake_extra_interface_libs**: List of extra libraries to be appended to "
"the generated CMake target's ``INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES``. Useful to declare "
"additional libraries (such as system libraries, or libraries located by the "
"packages declared in ``cmake_extra_dependencies``) that have to be linked "
"together with the package's own libraries. Can be defined both at the "
"package level and per-component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:254
msgid ""
"**cmake_link_feature**: Sets the link feature for the generated target. This "
"can be any of the built-in link features supported by CMake like "
"``WHOLE_ARCHIVE`` etc., or a custom one, provided you also set the expected "
"``CMAKE_LINK_LIBRARY_USING_<FEATURE>_SUPPORTED`` and "
"``CMAKE_LINK_LIBRARY_USING_<FEATURE>`` variables. (Possibly using the "
"**cmake_extra_variables** property). Supported when using CMake 3.24 or "
"newer. This property performs **no** checks on the given feature, it is up "
"to the recipe author to ensure that the feature is usable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:260
msgid ""
"**nosoname**: boolean value that should be used only by dependencies that "
"are defined as ``SHARED`` and represent a library built without the "
"``soname`` flag option. When set to ``True``, the generated target will have "
"the ``IMPORTED_NO_SONAME_<CONFIG>`` CMake property set to ``TRUE``, so CMake "
"skips the SONAME check when linking. Can be set at the package level or per-"
"component. Ignored for non-shared library types. Available since Conan 2.31."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:267
#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:483
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:269
msgid ""
"def package_info(self):\n"
"    ...\n"
"    # MyFileName-config.cmake\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_file_name\", \"MyFileName\")\n"
"    # Names for targets are absolute, Conan won't add any namespace to the "
"target names automatically\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_target_name\", \"Foo::Foo\")\n"
"    # Automatically include the lib/mypkg.cmake file when calling "
"find_package()\n"
"    # This property cannot be set in a component.\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_build_modules\", "
"[os.path.join(\"lib\", \"mypkg.cmake\")])\n"
"\n"
"    # Create a new target \"MyFooAlias\" that is an alias to the "
"\"Foo::Foo\" target\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_target_aliases\", [\"MyFooAlias\"])\n"
"\n"
"    # Skip this package when generating the files for the whole dependency "
"tree in the consumer\n"
"    # note: it will make useless the previous adjustments.\n"
"    # self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_find_mode\", \"none\")\n"
"\n"
"    # Add extra variables to the generated config file\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_extra_variables\", {\n"
"                                   \"FOO\": 42,\n"
"                                   \"CMAKE_GENERATOR_INSTANCE\": \"$"
"{GENERATOR_INSTANCE}/buildTools/\",\n"
"                                   \"CACHE_VAR_DEFAULT_DOC\": {\"value\": "
"\"hello world\",\n"
"                                                             \"cache\": "
"True, \"type\": \"STRING\"}\n"
"                               })\n"
"\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_link_feature\", \"WHOLE_ARCHIVE\")\n"
"    # Additional names that consumers of this library might usually use in "
"their find_package() calls,\n"
"    # so they can find the same config file with different lower/upper case "
"variants.\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_file_name_variants\", "
"[\"myfilename\", \"MYFILENAME\"])\n"
"\n"
"    # Emit ``find_dependency(MyOpenMPI REQUIRED)`` in the generated <pkg>-"
"config.cmake,\n"
"    # so consumers can locate dependencies not provided as Conan requires.\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_extra_dependencies\", "
"[\"MyOpenMPI\"])\n"
"\n"
"    # Append extra libraries to the generated target's "
"INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_extra_interface_libs\", "
"[\"MyOpenMPI::MyOpenMPI\"])\n"
"\n"
"# Or if using components\n"
"def package_info(self):\n"
"    self.cpp_info.components[\"mycomponent\"].set_property(\"cmake_target_name\", "
"\"Foo::Var\")\n"
"\n"
"    # Create a new target \"VarComponent\" that is an alias to the "
"\"Foo::Var\" component target\n"
"    self.cpp_info.components[\"mycomponent\"].set_property(\"cmake_target_aliases\", "
"[\"VarComponent\"])\n"
"\n"
"    # ``cmake_extra_interface_libs`` can also be set on a single component,\n"
"    # in which case it is appended only to that component's "
"INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES.\n"
"    self.cpp_info.components[\"mycomponent\"].set_property(\"cmake_extra_interface_libs\",\n"
"                                                         [\"MyOpenMPI::MyOpenMPI\"])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:321
msgid ""
"Using ``CMakeConfigDeps.set_property()`` method you can overwrite the "
"property values set by the Conan recipes from the consumer. This can be done "
"for every property listed above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:324
msgid ""
"class Pkg(ConanFile):\n"
"\n"
"    requires = \"zlib/1.3.1\"\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"    def generate(self):\n"
"        deps = CMakeConfigDeps(self)\n"
"        # This will require in CMakeLists.txt a\n"
"        # target_link_libraries(mytarget PUBLIC MyZlib::MyZlib)\n"
"        deps.set_property(\"zlib\", \"cmake_target_name\", "
"\"MyZlib::MyZlib\")\n"
"        deps.generate()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:340
msgid ""
"You can also use the ``set_property()`` method to invalidate the property "
"values set by the upstream recipe and use the values that Conan assigns by "
"default. To do so, set the value ``None`` to the property like "
"``deps.set_property(\"zlib\", \"cmake_target_name\", None)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:344
msgid ""
"After doing this the generated target name for the Zlib library will be "
"``zlib::zlib`` instead of ``ZLIB::ZLIB`` which is the upstream default "
"target name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:347
msgid ""
"Additionally, `CMakeConfigDeps.set_property()` can also be used for packages "
"that have components. In this case, you will need to provide the package "
"name along with its component separated by a double colon (`::`). Here's an "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:351
msgid ""
"def generate(self):\n"
"    deps = CMakeConfigDeps(self)\n"
"    deps.set_property(\"pkg::component\", \"cmake_target_name\", "
"<new_component_target_name>)\n"
"    deps.generate()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:362
msgid "Multiple CMake config files per package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:364
msgid ""
"By default, ``CMakeConfigDeps`` generates a single ``<name>-config.cmake`` "
"file per package, containing the targets of all its components. However, "
"some libraries distribute **several CMake packages** from a single project, "
"for example ``find_package(SPIRV-Tools)`` and ``find_package(SPIRV-Tools-"
"opt)``. To be able to model that from a single Conan package, use the "
"``cmake_file_names`` property (since Conan 2.34) to define which components "
"belong to which CMake config file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:369
msgid ""
"def package_info(self):\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_file_names\", {\n"
"        \"SPIRV-Tools\": {\"components\": [\"spirv-tools-core\"]},\n"
"        \"SPIRV-Tools-opt\": {\"components\": [\"spirv-tools-opt\"]},\n"
"        \"SPIRV-Tools-link\": {\n"
"            \"components\": [\"spirv-tools-link\"],\n"
"            # Properties that only apply to the SPIRV-Tools-link config "
"files\n"
"            \"properties\": {\"cmake_config_version_compat\": "
"\"ExactVersion\"},\n"
"        },\n"
"    })\n"
"\n"
"    self.cpp_info.components[\"spirv-tools-core\"].libs = [\"SPIRV-Tools\"]\n"
"    self.cpp_info.components[\"spirv-tools-opt\"].libs = [\"SPIRV-Tools-"
"opt\"]\n"
"    self.cpp_info.components[\"spirv-tools-opt\"].requires = [\"spirv-tools-"
"core\"]\n"
"    self.cpp_info.components[\"spirv-tools-link\"].libs = [\"SPIRV-Tools-"
"link\"]\n"
"    self.cpp_info.components[\"spirv-tools-link\"].requires = [\"spirv-tools-"
"core\", \"spirv-tools-opt\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:389
msgid ""
"The generator will create a complete set of files for each key (``SPIRV-"
"ToolsConfig.cmake``, ``SPIRV-Tools-optConfig.cmake``, ``SPIRV-Tools-"
"linkConfig.cmake``, their ``*Targets.cmake``, version files, etc.), and a "
"``<KEY>_DIR`` variable for each of them in ``conan_cmakedeps_paths.cmake``. "
"Consumers then use the ``find_package()`` of the CMake packages they need, "
"and link the component targets directly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:394
msgid "CMakeLists.txt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:394
msgid ""
"find_package(SPIRV-Tools-link CONFIG REQUIRED)\n"
"\n"
"add_executable(example src/main.cpp)\n"
"target_link_libraries(example PRIVATE SPIRV-Tools-link)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:402
msgid ""
"When a component of one config file requires components that live in other "
"config files (from the same or from other Conan packages), the generated "
"``<KEY>-config.cmake`` automatically calls ``find_dependency()`` on the "
"right config files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:405
msgid "When ``cmake_file_names`` is defined, these rules apply:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:407
msgid ""
"Every component of the package must be listed in exactly one of the files. A "
"``ConanException`` is raised if a component does not exist, or if it is not "
"added to any of the files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:409
msgid ""
"There is **no root config file** named after the package, and no root "
"``pkg::pkg`` target is created, so ``default_components`` are ignored. The "
"targets are not aggregated either, because each config file declares only "
"the targets of its own components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:412
msgid ""
"Consumers that require a package using ``cmake_file_names`` must declare "
"which component they link with, using ``self.cpp_info.requires = "
"[\"pkg::component\"]`` in their ``package_info()``. Otherwise, a "
"``ConanException`` is raised, because there is no ``pkg::pkg`` target to "
"link against."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:415
msgid "Each component must define at most one library in ``libs``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:416
msgid ""
"It takes precedence over ``cmake_file_name``, which is ignored if both "
"properties are defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:417
msgid ""
"Properties like ``cmake_build_modules``, ``cmake_extra_variables`` or "
"``system_package_version`` defined in the ``properties`` field of a file, "
"apply only to that file. The rest of properties are read as usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:419
msgid ""
"The legacy variables of each config file (like ``<KEY>_INCLUDE_DIRS`` or "
"``<KEY>_LIBRARIES``) only contain the information of the components of that "
"file. The ``<KEY>_VERSION_STRING`` is also generated for each file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:422
msgid ""
"Consumers can also redefine the file names and their components with "
"``CMakeConfigDeps.set_property()``, in the same way as any other property:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:425
msgid ""
"def generate(self):\n"
"    deps = CMakeConfigDeps(self)\n"
"    deps.set_property(\"spirv-tools\", \"cmake_file_names\", {\n"
"        \"SPIRV-Tools\": {\"components\": [\"spirv-tools-core\", \"spirv-"
"tools-opt\"]},\n"
"        \"SPIRV-Tools-link\": {\"components\": [\"spirv-tools-link\"]},\n"
"    })\n"
"    deps.generate()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:438
msgid ""
"``cmake_file_names`` cannot be set with ``deps.set_property(..., "
"build_context=True)`` for dependencies in the build context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:442
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:444
msgid ""
"Allows to define custom user CMake configuration besides the standard "
"Release, Debug, etc ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:446
msgid ""
"def generate(self):\n"
"    deps = CMakeConfigDeps(self)\n"
"    # By default, ``deps.configuration`` will be "
"``self.settings.build_type``\n"
"    if self.options[\"hello\"].shared:\n"
"        # Assuming the current project ``CMakeLists.txt`` defines the "
"ReleasedShared configuration.\n"
"        deps.configuration = \"ReleaseShared\"\n"
"    deps.generate()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:457
msgid ""
"The ``CMakeConfigDeps`` is a *multi-configuration* generator, it can "
"correctly create files for Release/Debug configurations to be simultaneously "
"used by IDEs like Visual Studio. In single configuration environments, it is "
"necessary to have a configuration defined, which must be provided via the "
"``cmake ... -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=<build-type>`` argument in command line "
"(Conan will do it automatically when necessary, in the ``CMake.configure()`` "
"helper)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:464
msgid "Using \"host\" and \"build\" context dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:466
msgid ""
"With ``CMakeConfigDeps``, it is possible to use executable ``IMPORTED`` "
"targets from regular \"host\" dependencies. This can only be done in case "
"where platform binary compatibility is possible, and in other cases like "
"cross-compiling, it will fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:468
msgid ""
"The ``IMPORTED`` executable targets will be automatically created from the "
"``self.cpp_info.exe`` and ``self.cpp_info.components[\"mycomponent\"].exe`` "
"information. These targets can be directly used by consumers in their own "
"builds as tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:470
msgid ""
"When a Conan package recipe depends on the same package both as regular "
"``requires`` and ``tool-requires``, to be able to implement scenarios like "
"cross-building, the \"build\" context will have priority when defining the "
"executable ``IMPORTED`` targets. A common example is when using ``protobuf`` "
"in a cross-building scenario, the ``protoc`` compiler inside the package "
"that is used for the \"host\" architecture cannot be executed in the current "
"\"build\" machine. So the recipe defines a ``self.requires(\"protobuf/"
"version\")`` and a ``self.tool_requires(\"protobuf/version\")``. In this "
"case, the library (headers, static/shared lib) targets will be obtained from "
"the dependency in the \"host\" context, but the executable target for "
"``protoc`` will be defined from the \"build\" context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:476
msgid ""
"Disable ``CMakeConfigDeps`` to use ``xxx-config.cmake`` files inside the "
"package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:478
msgid ""
"Some projects may want to disable the ``CMakeConfigDeps`` generator for "
"downstream consumers. This can be done by setting ``cmake_find_mode`` to "
"``\"none\"``. If the project wants to provide its own configuration targets, "
"it should append them to the ``builddirs`` attribute of ``cpp_info``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:481
msgid ""
"This method is intended to work with downstream consumers using the "
"``CMakeToolchain`` generator or by including the generated "
"``conan_cmakedeps_paths.cmake`` file, which will be populated with the "
"``builddirs`` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:485
msgid ""
"def package(self):\n"
"    ...\n"
"    cmake.install()\n"
"\n"
"def package_info(self):\n"
"    self.cpp_info.set_property(\"cmake_find_mode\", \"none\") # Do NOT "
"generate any files\n"
"    self.cpp_info.builddirs.append(os.path.join(\"lib\", \"cmake\", \"foo\"))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/cmake/cmakeconfigdeps.rst:497
msgid "Reference"
msgstr ""

